  "notes": "After the defense takes the first 3 heart tricks, and exits a club, South must take the balance. South's only concern is to avoid losing a trick to the ♠K. After drawing trump, South will be able to trump his ♦2 in the dummy.\n\nSouth could cash the ♠A. This play would work when either defender has a singleton ♠K (2 cases).\n\nSouth could instead finesse West for the ♠K, leading spades from South and playing low from dummy if West doesn't play the ♠K. This plan will work when West has either the singleton ♠K, doubleton ♠K6, doubleton ♠K7, or tripleton ♠K (4 cases).\n\nThe percentage play is, therefore, to take the spade finesse. When you have a 10 card fit, containing all the high cards except the King, finessing against the King is the percentage play.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
